    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d405">

                <pb facs="0496" n="1330" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1330"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 659.119/362k</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Denmark</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grant-Smith</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 22, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>926. The Danish commissioners have had a series of conferences with the War Trade
                    Board who have been very favorably impressed with the personnel of the
                    commission. The War Trade Board, during these conferences, have adhered to the
                    terms of the proposal of January 17.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d405-f1"/> The
                    Legation will be kept informed of any new developments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d405-f1" n="2" xml:id="d405-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 6297, Jan. 19, 1918, to the Ambassador in Great Britain, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg1299">p. 1299</ref>.</p>
            </note>
